      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E003",
        "passage_id": "P002",
        "quote": "The plaintiff commenced this action to recover damages for personal injuries he allegedly sustained when he slipped and fell on ice in a parking lot leased to the defendant Pro Park, Inc. (hereinafter Pro Park).",
        "statement_status": "allegation"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E004",
        "passage_id": "P002",
        "quote": "A property owner, or a party in possession or control of real property, will be held liable for an accident involving snow and ice on its property only when it created the dangerous condition that caused the accident or had actual or constructive notice of its existence",
        "statement_status": "court_finding"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E005",
        "passage_id": "P003",
        "quote": "Here, Pro Park demonstrated, prima facie, that it lacked constructive notice of the allegedly dangerous condition on which the plaintiff fell.",
        "statement_status": "court_finding"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E006",
        "passage_id": "P003",
        "quote": "Specifically, Pro Park demonstrated that no icy conditions existed in the parking lot at the time it was inspected just before closing at 9:00 p.m. the night before the accident, and that the plaintiff's accident occurred at approximately 5:30 a.m. the following morning, before the parking lot opened.",
        "statement_status": "court_finding"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E007",
        "passage_id": "P003",
        "quote": "Under the circumstances, Pro Park established that it did not have a reasonably sufficient period of time to remedy the allegedly dangerous condition prior to the plaintiff's accident",
        "statement_status": "court_finding"
      },
      {
        "evidence_id": "E008",
        "passage_id": "P003",
        "quote": "In opposition, the plaintiff failed to raise a triable issue of fact.",
        "statement_status": "court_finding"
      },
